# Backlog updates (`BACKLOG.md`)

When finishing work that matches an item in `BACKLOG.md`, update that file in the **same change** (or same PR/commit batch). Do not wait for the user to ask.

## When to update

- Closing or implementing a backlog bug/feature
- Discovering code already implements an open `[ ]` item
- Completing soak/verification with concrete evidence
- Deprioritizing or cancelling an item (note why briefly)

## Status conventions (match existing file)

- Open: `- [ ] Short description`
- Fixed in tree, not proven live: `- [x] … — **fixed** YYYY-MM-DD · **verified** pending`
- Verified: `- [x] … — **fixed** YYYY-MM-DD · **verified** YYYY-MM-DD (evidence: …)` then move to **Done (recent)** when appropriate
- Priority: prefix with `**Now**` only for 1–3 active items; clear `**Now**` when done or deprioritized

## Do / don't

- **Do** mark **fixed** when the implementation is in the tree (code review + tests OK).
- **Do not** mark **verified** from code review alone for live/paper/execution items — need log line, trade id, soak note, or explicit user confirmation.
- **Do not** invent backlog items for every tiny change; only track work that belongs in Bugs / Features / Testing / Ops.
- **Do not** dump ephemeral GA run metrics into `BACKLOG.md` — use `docs/strategy_research.md` or run reports under `results/`.
- Full audits of the whole backlog only when the user asks (or after a large milestone they request).

## Example

```markdown
# After implementing broker Stop deferral:
- [x] No STRATEGY SIGNAL EXIT + market while stop armed — **fixed** 2026-07-09 · **verified** pending

# After paper trade confirms:
- [x] … — **fixed** 2026-07-09 · **verified** 2026-07-10 (evidence: TRADE CLOSE Broker Stop @ … in paper log)
```
